        "prompt": "Solve $(x-3)(x+5)<0$ using the same method.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$-5<x<3$.",
          "worked": "For a negative product, the factors have opposite signs.\n\nCase 1:\n$$\\begin{align*}x-3&>0 & x+5&<0\\\\x&>3 & x&<-5\\end{align*}$$\nNo value satisfies both conditions.\n\nCase 2:\n$$\\begin{align*}x-3&<0 & x+5&>0\\\\x&<3 & x&>-5\\end{align*}$$\nThe combined interval is $-5<x<3$. The endpoints are excluded because the product is zero there.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 54
      }
